From f22fe3d080ef8b2205c1c21e6d2e828ba701f629 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 07:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Put the numeric tree's guard where the coercion was, item 3-1

The guarded tree reached 12.2% of the corpus's boxes against a census
ceiling of 86.6%, and nothing said which of its six eligibility
conditions was refusing the rest -- a numerator with no denominator,
which by the standing lessons is a claim about the instrument.

Counted with a refusal waterfall on the same terms as item 3-6's
(attribute each candidate to the FIRST condition it fails), 862 of 5 396
candidate arithmetic nodes specialize -- 16.0%. The two rules that turn
down the rest are one finding rather than two: `+` is left-associative,
so `a[0]+a[1]+a[2]+a[3]` refuses at the root as order-unsafe (1 762),
refuses again at each left child, and its bottom node is then a lone
operator with no saving to make (2 718). A chain of k operators produces
k-1 order-unsafe rows and one no-saving row and specializes nothing.

The sub-census then said the rule is not refusing what phase 3 assumed.
The blocking leaf is a property read 1 028 times and a computed element
read 34 -- 1.9% -- so after six items written around array-resident
data, the leaf that blocks the order rule is an object field, 984 of
them Box2D's.

Nothing required the leaves to move. The hoisting form is bounded by the
fact that it hoists: it evaluates every leaf into a temporary ahead of
one combined test, so a leaf crossing a coercion has to be pure.
Emitting each leaf at its own postorder position and putting the test
where the coercion it stands in for would have run preserves the
reference order exactly, and then the purity rule has nothing left to
protect -- the same soundness argument the hoisting form makes, read
from the other end. Each internal node carries a bool, a raw double and
a JSValue, so a failure part-way up boxes the accumulated double once
and lets the rest run generically, which the hoisting form cannot do.

Measured on the Octane corpus, one build, BROILER_JS_NUMERIC_TREE_ORDER
the only difference: generic arithmetic invocations 53 353 957 ->
6 626 052 (0.124x) and boxes 67 795 858 -> 31 162 330 -- 36 633 528
removed, 54.0% of everything the corpus allocates, against 12.2% for the
guarded tree, 9.4% for the ToNumeric reuse and 0.36% for the five locals
items combined. OrderUnsafe goes 1 762 -> 0 and NoSavingToMake
2 718 -> 1 181 without that rule being touched, which is the
chain-residue prediction coming out.

The leaf cap had to be re-measured too. It was 8 and had never fired,
because the order rule refused those trees first; at 16 it turns down 8
instead of 85 and the corpus loses a further 664 338 boxes, 2.1%. A
constant's measured cost is only valid for the configuration it was
measured in.

Wall clock, ABBA-interleaved at process granularity, six pairs, counters
off: driver 0.969x on six of six, NavierStokes 0.834x and Crypto 0.893x
both on six of six, against the two zero-box controls at 1.002x and
0.999x. Box2D removes 51% of its own boxes and reads 1.003x, because
that is 861 000 a second against NavierStokes' 6 500 000 -- the rate
lesson holding a second time. 54.0% of the allocation buys 3.1% of the
time.

NumericTreeOrderTests -- 11 fixtures, every value case on both settings
of the switch, so each is a statement about JavaScript rather than about
the fast path. Left-leaning chains of elements and of fields; a valueOf
that mutates a later leaf; a throwing coercion that must beat a later
leaf that would also throw, which is the sharpest one because both arms
throw and only the message says whether the order held; four getters
logging that every leaf is read once and left to right; a failure
half-way up that must leave the rest generic; a String defeating the
guard mid-chain; BigInt mixing from the middle; NaN, the infinities and
-0 carried across several nodes as raw doubles; ToInt32 wrapping at
every node; and a thousand-iteration element kernel. Plus three counter
assertions, because all eleven also pass when nothing specializes.

This also broke the guarded tree's own ATreeWhoseOrderCannotBePreserved-
IsRefused fixture, which is the fixture working: it asserted the refusal
this removes. Restated as a Theory on both settings asserting the
invariant -- the answer is 25 either way, and only which form computes
it moves.

Full repository suite 8 063 tests, 0 failures across 14 assemblies. All
five pinned test262 manifests run on both arms: the shipping arm is
identical to the recorded row manifest by manifest (8 710 / 8 617 / 84 /
251 / 9), and four of five agree file for file between the arms; on
`arrays` the control put one already-tracked integer-limit test in
`failed` rather than `timedOut`, with the set of 26 non-passing files
the same on both.
